{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779047700,"nonce":"7rj3Iu7eb2dXqxY6x42qOnWX4Is=","message":"## Status update before continuing Phase 2\n\nPhase 1 on the Feedbax side is now implemented and merged: `5429a23` closed via merge `947fc2489ee6`. That slice delivered the first provider/manifest substrate: manifest/provenance/artifact models, local content-addressed artifact storage plus rebuildable manifest index, provider capability/health/registry/validation Python + CLI + HTTP surfaces, and worker training-run manifest emission with artifact refs. The remaining Phase 1 limits are still the expected ones: registry snapshots wrap existing mechanisms, evaluation/analysis execution is not yet provider-driven, and training manifest retrieval is current-job scoped.\n\nMandible also has important foundation work landed since this roadmap was written:\n- `097d2b7` closed via merge `cfef20fc9d49`: canonical issue/work ledger, git-bug adapter, migration gates, operational links, graph projection, and shared issue-detail UI/API.\n- `10a4214`, `2b03ed3`, `67a12d9`, and `466847f` closed: unified Chat/History/app-shell work has moved Mandible toward the conversation-centered app shell. Remaining chat/app-shell follow-ups are now coordinated under Mandible `80f18c0`.\n\nI am resuming Phase 2 in Mandible now. The implementation target is the provider/artifact part of the roadmap, not more chat shell work: read the Mandible specs `de2f8ac` and `2472c51`, reuse or split concrete child issues where the current specs are too broad, then implement the next inspectable slice for Feedbax provider/manifest/artifact ingestion and graph/detail visibility.\n\nThe intended next slice is to make Mandible able to take a small Feedbax provider manifest plus training/eval/analysis manifest/artifact refs, persist them through Mandible-owned provider/artifact records, and expose them through the graph/detail APIs without hardcoding Feedbax internals. If the existing Mandible issues already cover that at the right level, I will reuse them; if not, I will add a concrete child issue before coding and cross-link it here.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}